# Cite the tagged release a result was produced with, never main: two runs are
# comparable only if their suite fingerprints match, and a fingerprint names the
# conditions of one release. CHANGELOG.md lists what each release moved.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use exchange-lab in research or teaching, please cite the tagged release you
  used, and report the suite fingerprint printed in each run's outcome.cfg.
title: "exchange-lab: a deterministic market simulator on a price-time-priority matching engine"
abstract: >-
  A price-time-priority exchange matching engine in C++20 and a seeded simulated market
  of strategies trading inside it, for teaching and researching market microstructure:
  paired experiments on fixed seed blocks, an evaluator with tested controls, and
  byte-for-byte reproduction of every run. The market is invented, so its results are
  statements about the simulation, not predictions about a real venue.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Philbert
    family-names: Poku
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-26
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/PhillysTheBest/exchange-lab"
url: "https://github.com/PhillysTheBest/exchange-lab/releases/tag/v1.0.0"
keywords:
  - market microstructure
  - matching engine
  - limit order book
  - agent-based simulation
  - reproducibility
  - C++20
